<item>
<title>[TPP-10568] SPIKE: Automate Treasury Trade Submission to FICC (RTTM Website)</title>
<link>https://jira.us.bank-dns.com/browse/TPP-10568</link>
<project id="15308" key="TPP">CT-TPP Operations, Pricing, Bonds &amp; Cash</project>
<description><h2><a name="Background%2FCurrentState"></a>Background / Current State</h2> <p>Treasury trade settlement for DVP, repo, cash buys, and cash sells is currently performed via <b>manual entry into the FICC RTTM website</b>, with each entry capped at <b>$50MM increments</b>. This process is labor‑intensive, error‑prone, and limits scalability as volumes increase.</p> <p>Internal discussions and prior problem statements already highlight that <b>FICC supports MQ messaging</b>, but this capability is not currently leveraged, resulting in continued reliance on manual workflows.</p> <h2><a name="ProblemStatement"></a>Problem Statement</h2> <p>Manual trade entry into FICC:</p> <ul> <li>Constrains throughput</li> <li>Increases operational risk and error rates</li> <li>Introduces settlement delays</li> <li>Will not scale with increased volumes driven by regulatory clearing mandates</li> <li><h2><a name="BusinessObjective"></a>Business Objective</h2></li> </ul> <p>Evaluate and define a <b>path to automate Treasury trade submission to FICC</b> by leveraging <b>FICC‑enabled MQ messaging</b>, eliminating manual RTTM entry and enabling scalable, controlled, and auditable settlement processing.<br/> <b>answer key feasibility and design questions</b> needed to decide <b>how</b> and <b>where</b> automation should occur.<br/>  </p> <p><b>How Traders Book the Trade on FICC</b></p> <p>Traders book into RTTM (By front office). The details are based off of trades completed with brokers so that's all manual. Usually a chat with brokers. What I will say though is when talking about buying or selling Treasuries, the traders book those in TOMS within Bloomberg - from there it will need to go into RTTM. </p> <ul> <li>Process mapping: <b>manual RTTM vs future automated flow</b></li> <li>Stakeholder identification (Business, Ops, Tech, FICC)</li> </ul> <p>video with business - <a href="https://usbank-my.sharepoint.com/personal/parshwa_s1_usbank_com/_layouts/15/guestaccess.aspx?share=IQDOMe9d_30LTaU-XQC8Ne7eAdoBnQNjvwQH2EW4bUohDTc&amp;e=akQovM" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Repo DVP Discussion-20260326_120119-Meeting Recording.mp4</a></p></description>
